.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt SYSCTL 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm sysctl
.Nd get or set kernel state
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl bdehiNnoqtx
.Op Fl f Ar filename
.Ar name Ns Op = Ns Ar value Ns Op , Ns Ar value
.Ar ...
.Nm
.Op Fl bdehNnoqtx
.Fl a
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads and sets the kernel's variables, the management information
base described in
.Xr sysctl 3 .
Each variable has a dotted name, such as
.Va kern.ostype ;
naming a node, such as
.Va kern ,
shows every variable under it.
A
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value
argument sets the variable, printing its old and new values.
Only the superuser may set variables, and only those that are writable;
tunables are fixed when the kernel starts and are set on the kernel command
line instead.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl a
Show every variable, except a few that are only read by name, such as
.Va kern.msgbuf ,
which
.Xr dmesg 8
shows.
.It Fl b
Write values as raw binary, with no names.
.It Fl d
Show each variable's description instead of its value.
.It Fl e
Separate names from values with
.Ql =
rather than
.Ql :\& .
.It Fl f Ar filename
Set the variables listed in
.Ar filename ,
in the format of
.Xr sysctl.conf 5 .
.It Fl h
Print numbers with thousands separators.
.It Fl i
Ignore unknown names silently.
.It Fl N
Show names only.
.It Fl n
Show values only.
.It Fl o
Show opaque values of an unknown structure, in hexadecimal.
.It Fl q
Report nothing but errors.
.It Fl t
Show each variable's type instead of its value.
.It Fl x
Show every value except strings in hexadecimal.
.El
.Pp
Structures are shown the way their fields read:
.Va kern.boottime
as seconds, microseconds and a date,
.Va kern.clockrate
as its rates,
.Va vm.loadavg
as the three averages, and
.Va vm.vmtotal
as a table of totals.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/sysctl.conf -compact
.It Pa /etc/sysctl.conf
variables set at boot
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Show the load average and the number of free pages:
.Pp
.Dl sysctl vm.loadavg vm.stats.vm.v_free_count
.Pp
Set the host name:
.Pp
.Dl sysctl kern.hostname=example
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sysctl 3 ,
.Xr sysctl.conf 5 ,
.Xr dmesg 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
utility first appeared in
.Bx 4.4 .
This one is OxideBSD's own, written in Rust after the one in
.Fx .
